implementationPlan.description:
REACHED THROUGH THE PRODUCTION LISTENER (DoD 2, and the half a handler-seam test cannot prove) — new `apps/daemon/src/daemon-entry-backups.test.ts`, copying `apps/daemon/src/daemon-entry-deployments-health.test.ts` (349 lines, landed in 29f5d723) as its shape. `daemon-entry-ops.test.ts:187` spells the composition chain out if you need a second reference.
START THE REAL DAEMON, FETCH THE ROUTE OVER HTTP, and assert:
(a) the three restore-proof states arrive over the wire BY VALUE — the whole chain from the persisted record to the frame, which is what a handler-seam arm cannot reach;
(b) **NOT_CHECKED ARRIVES AS NOT_CHECKED**, its own arm, because every link between the store and the wire is a place it could collapse into PROVEN (task rail 1);
(c) an unwired port refuses with its stable code and rostered layer rather than serving an empty or healthy frame;
(d) the method guard answers correctly for a non-GET;
(e) no connection string, credential or raw path appears in ANY response body on this route, success or failure — assert over the actual bytes, with a positive control.
**THE DAEMON THIS TEST STARTS, IT STOPS** (task rail 5, epic rail 4): tear down on every exit path including the failure ones, and assert the port is free afterwards. A test that leaks a listener or a port makes every later gate on this board inadmissible.
